(Bug #67 — the position table. #45's control `tests/376` proves a declared
 return reads back correctly in every position it refuses an undeclared one
 in, but every line of it returns a text; float, map and buffer were never
 exercised, and each was wrong in a different subset of these positions. This
 is 376's float/map/buffer twin.)

To 'give float'. Return a float, 2.5.
To 'give map'. Return a map, {"ann": 30}.
To 'give buffer'. a buffer called made is 16 bytes in size. Copy "bytes" to made. Return a buffer, made.
To 'give float of' with a number called factor. Return a float, 2.5.
To 'give map of' with a number called factor. Return a map, {"ann": 30}.
To 'give buffer of' with a number called factor. a buffer called made is 16 bytes in size. Copy "bytes" to made. Return a buffer, made.

(the bare zero-argument spelling — parses as a name, not a call)
Print 'give float'.
Print 'give map'.
Print 'give buffer'.

(the spelling with a connector — parses as a call)
Print 'give float of' with 1.
Print 'give map of' with 1.
Print 'give buffer of' with 1.

(a format hole)
Print "hole {'give float'} {'give map'} {'give buffer'}".

(a value declaration — the tag has to travel too)
a value called 'carried measure' is 'give float'.
Print 'carried measure'.
a value called 'carried ages' is 'give map'.
Print 'carried ages'.

(a list slot, and the whole list)
a list called items is [].
append 'give float' to items.
append 'give map' to items.
Print element 1 of items.
Print element 2 of items.
Print items.

(a map slot)
a map called outer is {}.
set outer's "inner" to 'give map'.
Print outer's "inner".

(a text initializer and a buffer sink — the sinks #44 unified)
a text called captured is "{'give map'}".
Print captured.
a buffer called sink is 64 bytes in size.
Copy "{'give buffer'}" to sink.
Print sink.
